# Step 1: OBJ inspection

Generated by `obj_inspect/inspect_obj.py`. Numbers in the scaled frame are in metres, REP-103 (X forward, Y left, Z up), origin at the wing leading edge root on the centreline.

## File

- vertices: 20100, polygon records: 20559, triangles after fan split: 35799
- object groups: 144 (hull, wing, flaps, ailerons, tail, nacelles, props, floats, gear, doors, plus about 100 small cockpit/instrument objects)
- bounding box (obj units): min [-9.905, -4.462, -14.393], max [9.89, 4.354, 14.393], size [19.795, 8.816, 28.785]
- units: metres at full scale. Size 19.80 x 28.79 x 8.82 (length x span x height) vs the real CL-415 19.82 x 28.63 x 8.98 m
- watertight: no. The merged mesh is open (36 of 144 groups are closed on their own; the hull, wing and nacelles are open shells). Fine for proportions, useless for volumes, which is another reason to rebuild in CAD.
- no .mtl file next to the obj (only referenced), materials ignored

## Orientation

- nose is -X (hull nose at x = -9.91, cockpit glazing at x = -7.63)
- up is +Y (fin tip at y = 4.35, keel at y = -3.99)
- left is +Z (flotteurG, G = gauche, sits at z = +13.21). Check: forward x up = right, (-X) x (+Y) = -Z, so left is +Z. Conversion to REP-103: x = -X, y = +Z, z = +Y (det = +1)

## Scale

- wingspan in the file: 28.785 (tip to tip of `ailes`, winglet caps included)
- scale factor to 2.51 m: **0.087198** (about 1:11.47)
- obj chord 3.577 m, constant from root to the tip cap (stations: 3.573, 3.573, 3.573, 3.573, 3.573, 3.573, 3.573, 3.573)
- scaled chord: **0.3119 m** vs spec 0.278 m, so the OBJ wing is 12.2 % wider than the spec. Aspect ratio: OBJ 8.05, spec 9.03.
- no taper in the OBJ, so the CAD wing uses a constant 0.278 m chord as the spec says
- wing incidence relative to the hull datum (X axis): 2.65 deg; OBJ section t/c about 0.153 (NACA 4417 is 0.17, so the OBJ is close to it)
- the CAD wing keeps the OBJ quarter-chord position and the narrower chord is centred on it, so the CAD leading edge sits 8.5 mm aft of the scaled OBJ leading edge

## What the OBJ contains

| obj group | what it is | used for |
|---|---|---|
| fuselage | boat hull + fin + wing root fairing | hull offsets, fin planform |
| ailes | wing (fixed part) incl. winglet caps | span, chord, incidence |
| voletG/D, aileronG/D | flaps, ailerons | aileron span and chord ratio |
| derive, profondeur | h-stab, split elevator | tail planform, hinge line |
| derive2 | tailplane finlets (two) | finlets on the h-stab |
| direction | rudder | hinge and trailing edge lines |
| moteurs, bolG/D, heliceG/D | nacelles, spinners, 4-blade props | nacelle stations, prop disc |
| flotteurG/D | wingtip floats + pylons | float stations, pylon |
| roue*, axe*, trappe*, porte* | landing gear, doors | not modelled |
| ~100 cockpit objects | instruments, seats | not modelled |

Nothing the spec asks for is missing from the OBJ. The finlets (derive2) are not in the requested part list, so they are modelled as part of the h-stab body.

## Key proportions after scaling (REP-103, m)

- hull: nose x = 0.595, stern x = -1.092, keel z = -0.310, deck z = -0.017, max half beam 0.117, planing step at x = -0.140
- nacelles at y = +/-0.297, prop disc diameter 0.355 m, 4 blades, prop plane x = 0.190, axis z = 0.061
- floats at y = +/-1.152, float bottom z = -0.182
- h-stab: LE x = -0.813, hinge x = -0.957, TE x = -1.052, half span 0.468, chord line z = 0.127, t/c 0.164
- fin: root z = -0.017, tip z = 0.417, LE sweep 34.7 deg, hinge sweep 13.5 deg, t/c 0.117
- ailerons from y = 0.793 to 1.195, chord ratio 0.251

